{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming bfb8dfcc. I re-derived the defect on current main 7e7b8412 before promising, because the request describes it at a7a9abe7 and main has moved twice since.\n\nIt is still there and still exactly as described. internal/custody/custody.go:109 takes the disputed branch on len(completedSagas) \u003e 1 and marks every record of every completed saga Disputed, and it does so before any ownership test. The only ownership check, saga.offer.Body.From != owner at :121, sits inside the len == 1 branch and is therefore unreachable whenever a second completed saga exists. A saga is \"completed\" once it has a settlement referencing one acceptance referencing one offer with matching parties and authority logs -- none of which requires the offeror to hold the asset. So one legitimate owner-authorized transfer plus one fully shaped saga from a non-owner poisons both: the real transfer never settles and the asset reads Disputed.\n\nI will make the non-owner saga ineffective before competition is judged, so that only owner-authorized settlements can compete. I will preserve Disputed where multiple owner-authorized settlements genuinely compete, and preserve sequential transfer semantics where ownership legitimately moves more than once. The kernel/application boundary stays where it is.\n\nTests: one legitimate plus one non-owner saga; multiple legitimate competing settlements; sequential ownership changes. I will confirm by mutation that each new assertion fails when the behaviour it names is broken, rather than trusting that a green suite means the case is covered. Gates: focused and full Go tests with -race, vet, gofmt, git diff --check. Then an exact-head internal/custody artifact -- the path currently carries no live artifact -- and an independent review request carrying Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.\n\nBranch request/custody-owner-filter in its own worktree, as the request records.","body":{"area":"internal/custody","base":"7e7b8412bcd95e3d3345a481b72febc502513109","branch":"request/custody-owner-filter","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c66dc8f2770559c0f1b966a23f3233e9bfb8dfcc"}}